Original commit body from 43be54ba55d68abbe870cc1808da14a0ef4c0e3a:

The mapper exists because a PR touching only scripts/* or
.agent/hooks/_shared/* produces no reverse-slice, so ci.yml skips pytest
entirely. Its rule was 1:1 and exact -- scripts/<name> ->
tests/test_<name>.py with hyphens collapsed -- which reached one test per
script and left every sibling selected by nothing.

The rule is now a separator-insensitive prefix match. scripts/auto-pr
goes from 1 test to 11, bakeoff-deep from 1 to 6, agent-supervisor 1 to 2.

Both halves are load-bearing and the obvious one is wrong. Plain
prefix-matching -- the fix as filed, asserted to "pick up all ten
immediately" -- picks up zero: auto-pr collapses to auto_pr while its
tests are named test_autopr_*, and test_autopr_x does not start with
test_auto_pr. Prefix alone moves 27 -> 43 and leaves the motivating case
at 0. Dropping separators before comparing is what fixes it.

_shared/ now accepts .sh as well as .py. That directory holds 13 shell
helpers against 8 Python ones, so requiring .py left most of a covered
directory unreachable -- test_touch_heartbeat.py was dark despite
_shared/touch_heartbeat.sh sitting beside it. scripts/lib/ stays
unmapped; that one IS a recorded decision in the module docstring.

Severity stated accurately: this is a feedback-latency gap, not a
coverage hole. full-suite.yml's test-agent-infra job runs `pytest tests/`
twice daily, so these tests were never unrun -- they were unrun BEFORE
merge, so a regression could sit on dev for ~12 hours.

Testing: five tmp-tree tests for the new rule, plus a two-sided
reachability ratchet measured against the real tree -- a new unreachable
test fails, and an exempt test that becomes reachable also fails so the
list cannot rot. The 18 exemptions carry a verified reason each. The
mapper's existing tests deliberately use isolated tmp trees, which is
exactly why this survived: nothing ever compared the mapping against the
repo's real filenames, so the unit was correct while the wiring was inert.

Widening surfaces latent tests: scripts/contribute previously mapped to
nothing and now reaches test_contribute_github.py, which fails wherever
gh is installed (its harness prepends to PATH instead of replacing it, so
"WhenGhAbsent" never makes gh absent and the real binary hits the live
API). Verified pre-existing on clean dev in an isolated worktree; CI
runners have no gh so this does not break CI. Filed as WI-kahoj.

